{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Honor your father and your mother.</b> Until now He warned concerning the honor of the first, supernal Father, may He be blessed, and now He wished to seal the tablet with the honor of the latter, lower father, and said: just as I commanded you concerning My honor, so do I command you today concerning the honor of your father and your mother, for they are partners with Me in your formation. And the verse left it unspecified and did not spell out what this honor is, for it is to be learned from the honor of the first Father, may He be exalted. And just as He mentioned concerning the first Father, may He be blessed, that one should acknowledge Him and His existence — that He is one's Elohim — so one is obligated to acknowledge those who begot him, who are his father and his mother. And just as He mentioned ״לא יהיה לך״ — that one should not deny Him, so one is obligated not to deny his father, by saying of another man that he is his father; and one is further obligated not to swear by the name of his father or by the life of his father, falsely or in vain; and not to serve him on account of an inheritance of wealth or an inheritance of honor and prominence. And furthermore, included in the honor are things we have been commanded concerning, which the Sages explained: feeding him, giving him drink, clothing him, covering him, bringing him in and taking him out. And know that the language of honor applies to wealth, in the manner of (Proverbs 3) ״כבד את ה׳ מהונך״ — 'honor HaShem from your wealth'; and the honor that a person gives to the Holy One, blessed be He, with his wealth is that he give charity to the poor and separate terumah and tithes and gleanings and forgotten sheaves and pe'ah; and likewise with his father he is obligated in this — to give him from his wealth for all the aforementioned matters in which he is obligated toward his father; in all of them he is obligated to give if his father does not have. And as for the fact that Scripture fixed the reward for honor as length of days, the Gaon Rav Saadiah, of blessed memory, gave a reason for this: because sometimes the fathers are destined to live with the sons a long time, and the fathers are a heavy burden upon the sons, and the honoring weighs heavily upon them; therefore He fixed for them the reward of this commandment: ״למען יאריכון ימיך״ — 'so that your days be lengthened' — that is to say, you are obligated to honor them and you shall live with them, and if perhaps you suffer distress on account of their lives, know that it is upon your own life that you suffer distress — end of his words. Here you have these five utterances, the first ones, which were on one tablet and are linked one to another. Thus He commanded in the first utterance to believe in His divinity and His existence, in Him alone; and lest a person say that he believes in Him in partnership, therefore He immediately needed to forbid partnership and said ״לא יהיה לך אלהים אחרים״; and lest a person say: since partnership is forbidden, I may therefore take His name in vain — for this reason He warned concerning the honor of His name and said ״לא תשא״; and after He warned concerning the honor of His name, He warned concerning the honor of the Sabbath and said ״זכור את יום השבת״, for the remembrance of the Sabbath is His honor; and after He warned concerning the honor of the Sabbath, He warned concerning the honor of those who beget and said ״כבד את אביך ואת אמך״. I have explained for you the five first utterances that were on the first tablet, and I have made known to you their explanation and their linkage one to another."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:42.697162621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}